      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix a speculative decoding configuration bug where an explicitly selected `mtp` method is overwritten based on keywords in the draft model's path.\n\nIn `SpeculativeConfig.__post_init__`, a checkpoint directory containing `DFlash2` is classified as `dflash` even with `--speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":3}'`. This incorrectly initializes the EAGLE/DFlash config and can fail with `AttributeError: 'Qwen3_5Config' object has no attribute 'vocab_size'`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Preserve an explicitly selected `mtp` during automatic name-based speculative method detection, consistent with the existing `eagle`, `eagle3`, `dflash`, and `dspark` exceptions.\n- Add parametrized regression coverage for checkpoint directory names containing `dflash2`, `eagle3`, and `dspark`.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nOn vLLM v0.32.0, run a Qwen3.5-family model with an MTP head using a local model directory whose basename contains `DFlash2`:\n\n```bash\nvllm serve /models/qwen-mtp-DFlash2 \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":3}'\n```\n\n**Before:** `mtp` is overwritten by `dflash`; EAGLEConfig accesses a nonexistent top-level `vocab_size`.\n\n**After:** The explicitly chosen `mtp` method is retained. Renaming the local checkpoint directory to exclude `DFlash2` was confirmed to work on the affected deployment prior to this fix.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced on a real vLLM 0.32.0 deployment; renaming the checkpoint directory resolved startup.\n- Added focused regression tests (CI pending; not run locally in this environment).\n\n## AI assistance\n\nAI assistance was used to investigate the root cause and draft the patch and tests.",
