                  "body": "Adding `\"mtp\"` here fixes the name match, but it also skips the MTP branch below for anyone who sets the method explicitly. That branch is where the DeepSeek V4.1 check lives, the one that raises and says to use `dspark`, plus the `num_speculative_tokens > 1` warning. Before this, an explicit `\"mtp\"` fell through to it, and the comment in `hf_config_override` still says `method=\"mtp\"` on V4.1 \"is rejected below\". It also means `\"mtp\"` on a model that isn't an MTP type now passes here instead of hitting the `NotImplementedError`.\n\nCould you keep the name checks from overriding mtp but still run that branch? Skipping the eagle/dflash/dspark name checks when `self.method == \"mtp\"` would do it. A test with a `deepseek_v41` target and `method=\"mtp\"` would pin it.\n",
                  "createdAt": "2026-10-27T18:02:16Z",
                  "databaseId": 4392339355,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -1393,11 +1393,13 @@ def __post_init__(self):\n                 )\n \n                 # Automatically detect the method\n+                # Explicit methods take precedence over name-based inference.\n                 if self.method in (\n                     \"eagle\",\n                     \"eagle3\",\n                     \"dflash\",\n                     \"dspark\",\n+                    \"mtp\",",
